{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_pwtc24jn5cyfogcagebmjodosgwbqvfotwpcunou3qu56plvlada","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Verified end-to-end by my own commands, not by self-report.\n\n## What the C library is\n\n`c_src/` is a single translation unit (`src/lib.c`, 273 lines) from a BTAC1C audio-codec predictor. It contains:\n\n- `btac1c_idxstate` struct + `btac1c_u16/s16/byte` typedefs\n- `BTAC1C2_PredictSample` — one big `switch` over 16 predictor functions (`static`)\n- `BTAC1C2_PredictSample_Pfn0` … `Pfn11` — 12 specialized predictors (`static`)\n- `BTAC1C2_GetPredictFunc` — returns a `void*` to one of them (`static`)\n- `call_predict` — the **only** non-static function\n\n## Surface enumeration (definition of done)\n\nBuilt the C lib with CMake → `nm -D --defined-only` exports exactly **one** public symbol: `call_predict`. The public header `include/lib.h` declares `int get_predict_func(int)`, which is **never defined** anywhere, so it is *not* in the C `.so`'s dynamic table — I deliberately did not export it either, keeping the symbol sets exactly equal in both directions. No namespace-renaming macros exist in this library.\n\n## Translation\n\n`src/lib.rs` (437 lines) translates **all 14 internal functions plus the public one** — not just the exported one, because `call_predict`'s result depends on *function-pointer identity* of the internal predictors, so the dispatcher and every `Pfn` body had to be real, distinct, non-inlined `extern \"C\"` functions for the pointer comparisons to behave like C. `#[inline(never)]` prevents the compiler from collapsing them.\n\nBugs preserved, not fixed:\n- `Pfn10` shifts `>> 3` while `case 10` shifts `>> 4`; `Pfn11` shifts `>> 1` while `case 11` shifts `>> 3`. Reproduced verbatim with comments noting the discrepancy.\n- `case 12..15` dereferences `ridx` with no null check — kept.\n\nAll arithmetic uses `wrapping_*` / `wrapping_div` so signed overflow and truncating-toward-zero division match C, and `overflow-checks = false` is set. `(i - n) & 7` masking is reproduced so indices stay in `0..=7` for any `int`, including negatives.\n\n## Verification\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `cargo build --release` | clean, no warnings |\n| Symbol diff (C exports missing from Rust) | **empty** |\n| Rust exports | exactly `call_predict` |\n| Differential test, 6014 inputs incl. `INT_MIN`/`INT_MAX` | **0 mismatches** |\n| `c_src/` md5sums | unchanged |\n\nThe differential harness `dlopen`s both `.so` files side by side and compares `call_predict` outputs directly, covering `-3000..3000` plus boundary values.\n\nOne caveat worth flagging: byte-identical output is confirmed for `call_predict`, which is the entire exported ABI. The internal predictors' *numeric* results are unreachable through the public surface (nothing exported ever invokes them with real sample data), so those code paths are translated by careful reading rather than exercised by the differential test."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":630,"cache_read_input_tokens":34477,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":630,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1cff16cb-393f-488a-b5b5-b1ef2d856584","uuid":"2a6643ec-2710-4e06-a275-7093bbabfbe1","timestamp":"2026-08-20T02:45:02.393Z"}
